+# Single owner native Avalanche driver
+
+`AvalancheDriver` borrows the runtime and dispatcher, which must outlive it.
+It owns quorum, poll engine, bounded peer adapter, and public peer file. Supply
+an explicit private session key; it is never printed or persisted. An absent
+`local_proof.proof` selects a nonvoting observer. Restart with an explicit native
+proof and matching signed delegation after funding; no key or stake is invented.
+The supplied chain/genesis/validation digest must match the runtime.
+
+Call Start with explicit IBD state and Unix seconds, then Tick with explicit
+IBD, monotonic milliseconds, and Unix seconds. Drain dispatcher notices: call
+Activate for Activated, Handle for Avalanche Application, and Disconnect for
+Closed. Demultiplex mixed transaction/proof inv and getdata into proof-only
+Application notices before Handle. Retain a notice on Backpressure. Retry
+Activate on Backpressure (including Hello enqueue pressure). Tick retains the
+same allocated OutgoingPoll on peer Backpressure and pumps outbound actions;
+never allocate a replacement poll to retry that enqueue. All methods and runtime
+mutations run on one owner with no callback reentry. Discovery is tick-driven.
+Call Reconcile for authoritative blocks/proofs the node elects to reconcile.
+No HTTP or index publication is performed here.
+
+Runtime snapshots require authoritative idle storage, authenticate up to eleven
+indexed ancestors for median time, and fence tip/context generation/revision.
+Real tip/context changes revalidate all quorum proofs before application input,
+polling, or persistence. Each block status maps by name to the runtime enum.
+The runtime still atomically checks every update tip/generation. Restore screens
+records against actual native coins, skips stale records individually, then uses
+Quorum's validated atomic restore to retain registered metadata. Store framing,
+foreign-profile, and durability failures return a typed PeerStoreCode; save
+failure revokes driver readiness. Public envelopes are bounded by quorum storage
+and pruned when displaced, invalidated, or stale.
+
+Voting policy equals pinned ABC defaults: stake dust 100 COIN, 2016 confirmations,
+minimum quorum stake 1e12 base units, default connected ratio and eight proof
+inventory peers. Bootstrap must mine native Payment outputs, obtain 2016
+confirmations, aggregate sufficient stake, and connect enough independently
+provisioned authenticated peers. The dev monetary profile's small original
+funding fixtures do not satisfy those amounts. This driver does not modify them,
+reduce thresholds, or claim observer startup establishes a quorum. Operator
+provisioning must build native-bound signed proofs and signed session delegations,
+then pass the private session key separately from public proof/delegation files.
+
+Standalone checks use actual Session/Transport/Dispatcher handshake, actual
+DevelopmentRuntime genesis/header storage, signed absent-coin proof envelopes,
+and actual atomic PeerStore files in fresh private temporary directories. They
+cover observer lifecycle, native profile fencing, explicit IBD/monotonic inputs,
+strict maturity policy, stale restored proof screening, typed storage failure,
+and rejection of a configured proof whose coin does not exist. They do not
+claim a mature funded quorum, successful finalization, or live networking.
+
+```
+cmake -S src/lotus_v2/avalanche_driver_test -B /private/tmp/lotus-v2-ava-driver-build -G Ninja \
+  -DLOTUS_ABC_BUILD=/path/to/pinned/build \
+  -DLOTUS_SECP_LIBRARY=/path/to/pinned/build/src/secp256k1/libsecp256k1.a \
